auto_trader.py (1)
50-55: Daily-limit locking still allows overspending; make check + increment atomic

The new daily_limit_lock and guarded checks are a good step, but there’s still a race:

Two concurrent process_token_alert calls can both:
Pass the initial limit check under the lock.
Compute amount_sol.
Pass the second daily_auto_buy_spent + amount_sol check under the lock.
Because daily_auto_buy_spent is only incremented later (in a separate locked block after the trade succeeds), both paths can execute and push total spent beyond auto_buy_daily_limit_sol.
To enforce the daily cap strictly, the second check and the increment need to be in the same critical section, ideally with rollback if the trade fails. Conceptually:

