trader.py (2)
228-341: Quote-analysis uses wrong key names (outputAmount vs output_amount), breaking routing logic

_analyze_quotes, _calculate_quote_score, _check_split_routing, and _is_split_beneficial all assume camelCase keys:

quote['outputAmount']
quote.get('priceImpactPct', 0)
But all DEX adapters (JupiterDEX, RaydiumDEX, OrcaDEX) return snake_case keys:

output_amount
price_impact
This means:

_analyze_quotes will crash with KeyError or silently produce wrong scores/savings.
Split-routing (_check_split_routing, _is_split_beneficial) will also miscompute or fail.
You should standardize on the existing snake_case keys in the router:

