🧹 Nitpick comments (2)
trader.py (1)
376-384: Cleanup paths look good; consider tightening broad exception catches

The new SmartOrderRouter.close() and Trader.cleanup() correctly close all DEX sessions and log failures, which addresses the aiohttp session leak for long-running processes.

Both methods catch a bare Exception, which Ruff flags (BLE001). Given these are shutdown/cleanup paths, broad catching is acceptable, but if you want to satisfy the linter and be stricter you could:

Narrow to expected aiohttp / network errors, or
Add a comment / # noqa: BLE001 to explicitly document the intent not to let cleanup failures crash the process.
Functionally the current behavior is fine; this is mostly lint/noise.

Also applies to: 1160-1167

